Z||000000||86SE||06-01-2000||02:23 AM||||When ever I goto brake there is a clicking noise (one click) in the left front wheel.  It happens when the brakes are unused for at least 30 seconds.  When it clicks, I can feel it in the pedal.  <P>Is this a sticking piston in the caliper??||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phaeton||06-01-2000||03:55 AM||||Sliders or anti rattle clip? <BR>Sticking pistons usually stick both ways and leave black dust all over the wheel.<BR>Who did the brake job? if you did it yourself do you remember the piston moving smoothly when pushed into the caliper? New pads put the piston further into the hole and sometimes there is a built up ridge where the piston rode with the old thin pads.||||reg||12
